Imports:
  - Types:
      - JobManager
    From: app/src/main/java/org/thoughtcrime/securesms/jobmanager
  - Types:
      - DatabaseObserver
    From: app/src/main/java/org/thoughtcrime/securesms/database
  - Types:
      - LiveRecipientCache
    From: app/src/main/java/org/thoughtcrime/securesms/recipients
  - Types:
      - BillingApi
    From: core/util/src/main/java/org/signal/core/util/billing
  - Types:
      - SignalServiceMessageSender
      - SignalServiceMessageReceiver
      - SignalServiceAccountManager
    From: lib/libsignal-service/src/main/java/org/whispersystems/signalservice/api

Annotations: |
  This cell is the app-wide static service locator: every cross-cutting singleton the rest of
  the app module needs (job execution, database change notifications, the recipient cache, the
  billing backend, the network/protocol clients) is read through this one object rather than
  passed down through constructors. Every property is backed by a lazy delegate resolved through
  the nested Provider interface supplied to init — the production implementation of
  Provider (outside this cell) is what actually constructs each singleton, so this cell itself
  contains no construction logic, only the wiring/caching contract. This is the sole root of the
  dependency graph in this forest: nothing else documented here imports from it.

---

"AppDependencies()":
  location: AppDependencies.kt
  annotations: |
    Location for storing and retrieving every application-scoped singleton. init must be
    called once, early in Application.onCreate, before any property below is read; reading a
    property before init throws.
  methods:
    "init(application: Application, provider: Provider)": |
      Installs `application` and provider and bootstraps the sibling per-module dependency
      objects (CoreUtilDependencies, CoreUiDependencies, MediaSendDependencies, and others)
      using adapter Provider implementations backed by this same provider. A second call
      after the first is a no-op.
    "resetProtocolStores()": |
      Discards cached protocol-store-derived state so it is re-read from provider on next
      access — used after an operation that invalidates in-memory protocol state (e.g. changing
      accounts).
    "resetNetwork()": |
      Disconnects the websockets and discards every network-dependent singleton so the next
      access rebuilds them from current configuration; the websocket objects themselves survive
      and simply reconnect using the fresh configuration.
    "startNetwork()": |
      Opens the network connections needed for the app to send/receive live traffic.
  properties:
    "isInitialized -> Boolean": |
      Whether init has been called yet.
    "application -> Application": |
      The installed application instance.
    "jobManager -> JobManager": |
      The single, process-wide `JobManager` (from Imports) used to enqueue all background work.
    "databaseObserver -> DatabaseObserver": |
      The single, process-wide `DatabaseObserver` (from Imports) every table in the database
      cell notifies through.
    "recipientCache -> LiveRecipientCache": |
      The single, process-wide `LiveRecipientCache` (from Imports) backing Recipient.live().
    "billingApi -> BillingApi": |
      The active `BillingApi` (from Imports) implementation for this build/account, selected by
      whichever Provider implementation is installed.
    "signalServiceMessageSender -> SignalServiceMessageSender": |
      The single outbound-message client (from Imports), rebuilt whenever resetNetwork runs.
    "signalServiceMessageReceiver -> SignalServiceMessageReceiver": |
      The single attachment/media retrieval client (from Imports).
    "signalServiceAccountManager -> SignalServiceAccountManager": |
      The single account-management client (from Imports).
    "incomingMessageObserver -> IncomingMessageObserver": |
      Owns the persistent connection that receives new messages as they arrive.
    "signalCallManager -> SignalCallManager": |
      Coordinates the lifecycle of ongoing voice/video calls.
    "expiringMessageManager -> ExpiringMessageManager": |
      Schedules and performs deletion of messages whose disappearing-message timer has elapsed.
    "megaphoneRepository -> MegaphoneRepository": |
      Data source for in-app announcement banners ("megaphones").
    "okHttpClient -> OkHttpClient": |
      The shared HTTP client used for non-protocol network calls.

"AppDependencies.Provider()":
  location: AppDependencies.kt
  annotations: |
    The extension point a build variant implements and passes to init to actually construct
    every singleton AppDependencies exposes; this cell only declares the shape of that
    contract, not any implementation of it.
  methods:
    "provideJobManager(configurationBuilder: JobManager.Configuration.Builder) -> jobManager:JobManager": |
      Constructs the process-wide `JobManager` (from Imports).
    "provideDatabaseObserver() -> observer:DatabaseObserver": |
      Constructs the process-wide `DatabaseObserver` (from Imports).
    "provideRecipientCache() -> cache:LiveRecipientCache": |
      Constructs the process-wide `LiveRecipientCache` (from Imports).
    "provideBillingApi() -> api:BillingApi": |
      Constructs (or selects the no-op form of) the active `BillingApi` (from Imports) for this
      build/account.
    "provideSignalServiceMessageSender(protocolStore: SignalServiceDataStore, pushServiceSocket: PushServiceSocket, messageApi: MessageApi, keysApi: KeysApi) -> sender:SignalServiceMessageSender": |
      Constructs the outbound-message client (from Imports).
    "provideSignalServiceMessageReceiver(pushServiceSocket: PushServiceSocket) -> receiver:SignalServiceMessageReceiver": |
      Constructs the attachment/media retrieval client (from Imports).
    "provideSignalServiceAccountManager(authWebSocket: SignalWebSocket.AuthenticatedWebSocket, accountApi: AccountApi, pushServiceSocket: PushServiceSocket, groupsV2Operations: GroupsV2Operations) -> manager:SignalServiceAccountManager": |
      Constructs the account-management client (from Imports).

